To fix a slow fixture without inflating the timeout for every test, you can provide a separate timeout specifically for that fixture when defining it using `test.extend()`. This allows you to keep the overall test timeout small while granting the slow fixture additional time.

You can implement this by passing an options object with a `timeout` property as the second argument to the fixture definition:

